<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar finishes marginally easier.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar finishes marginally easier.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE white sugar ended slightly weaker after a rangebound day.</p>
<p>Front-month August ended 50 cents softer at $320.20 per tonne, just 10 cents off its low, while October finished 40 cents easier at $309.90.</p>
<p>Volume was 3,386 lots, with 2,532 lots in the front month.</p>
<p>In Paris, August and October closed 50 cents weaker at $320.0 and $310.0 respectively.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
</text>
